# cafe-ecs Architecture

C++ ECS game (SDL3 + Box2D + bagel). All game code in `namespace cafe`. No exceptions — use `assert` for programmer errors, `assertFatal` for unrecoverable failures.

## Components & Storage

- One header per component in `src/component/` — struct + `bagel::Storage<>` specialization after `namespace cafe` closes.
- Data struct → `SparseStorage<T>`; empty tag → `TaggedStorage<T>`.
- Umbrella: `#include "Components.h"`. Storage specializations live at global scope.

```cpp
namespace cafe { struct Health { int points{}; }; }

template <>
struct bagel::Storage<cafe::Health> final : bagel::NoInstance
{
    using type = bagel::SparseStorage<cafe::Health>;
};
```

## Systems & Factories

- Systems: free functions in `src/system/` (grouped by cohesion). Umbrella: `Systems.h`. No system-to-system calls — use components.
- Factories: `src/entity/*Factory.{h,cpp}` construct entities via `ent.addAll(...)`. No game logic. Umbrella: `Entities.h`.

## Coordinate System

- **World**: meters, Y-up (Box2D). **Screen**: logical pixels, Y-down (`LOGICAL_W`×`LOGICAL_H` in `GameConfig.h`).
- World↔screen math lives in `component/Transform.h` (`worldToScreenPoint`, `transformToFrect`, Box2D helpers). Do not duplicate elsewhere.

## Key Utilities

| Utility | Location | Use |
|---------|----------|-----|
| `WorldPos` | `src/WorldPos.h` | `{x, y}` world points without a full `Transform` |
| `RenderContext` | `src/RenderContext.h` | Global SDL window/renderer |
| `PhysicsContext` | `src/PhysicsContext.h` | `b2WorldId` singleton + step |
| `assertFatal` | `src/Utils.h` | Unrecoverable failures — log, message box, exit |

## Assets

Sprites in `res/`: `bg.png`, `counter.png`, `cup.png`, `machine.png`, `particle.png`, `def_customer.png`.
